course: dictionary
lesson: 14464
title: Words from the kitchen and the garden
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A parsnip is a vegetable, but you may not know the word yet. Context helps you find its meaning. «We roasted the parsnips with the carrots for Sunday dinner.» The words roasted, carrots and dinner tell you that a parsnip is something you cook and eat.
explain: Look for the clues about shape and taste. «After the frost, the parsnips tasted sweeter.» Sweeter tells you that the parsnip is eaten, and frost tells you it grows outside in the cold. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Some words are used in sayings. «Dad said, "Fine words butter no parsnips," when I promised to tidy my room but still did not.» Here parsnips is not about food at all. The saying means talk alone does not get things done. Pay attention to what the whole sentence is about.
fact: A parsnip is a long, pale cream root vegetable.
fact: A parsnip is shaped like a carrot, but it is cream-coloured.
fact: Parsnips are often roasted with Sunday dinner or Christmas dinner in the UK and Ireland.
fact: Parsnips grow underground, and frost makes them taste sweeter.
fact: «Fine words butter no parsnips» means talk alone does not get things done.
exercise: «We roasted the parsnips with the carrots for Sunday dinner.» What is a parsnip? | A farm animal | A type of bread | A small red fruit that grows on trees | *A long, pale cream root vegetable
exercise: «After the frost, the parsnips tasted sweeter.» Why did the parsnips taste sweeter? | Frost turns parsnips into bread | *Frost makes parsnips sweeter | Parsnips are always eaten raw in the snow | Parsnips only taste sweet on rainy days
exercise: Mum said, «Fine words butter no parsnips.» What does she mean? | *Talk alone does not get things done | Words are very expensive to buy | Parsnips can talk if you are kind to them | Butter is the best thing to put on parsnips
test: A parsnip is shaped like a... | banana | potato | pea | *carrot
test: Which meal do people often roast parsnips for in the UK and Ireland? | *Sunday dinner | Picnic lunch | Breakfast cereal | Birthday tea
exam: Which sentence is true about a parsnip? | *It is a long, pale cream root vegetable that tastes sweet when cooked | It is a loud bird that sings at night | It is a type of cheese made from milk | It is a red fruit that grows high in trees
